SUMMARY:Wissahickon Weird Loop Hike!
DESCRIPTION:Metrotrails: NJ\, PA\, NY Metropolitan Area Hiking and More!\n
 Join us for this very diverse loop hike\, the next in our Wissahickon Wate
 rshed series!\nThis will not only cover the next bit of the Wissahickon Gr
 een Ribbon\, we will also cover lots of other trails in area parks we have
 n't done yet.\nWe meet at the long parking area with the restroom across f
 rom the Hawk Watch on St Park Rd in Fort Washington State Park. From here\
 , we'll go slightly south and follow one of the trails in that section of 
 the park.\nWe will weave around and make our way along some of the trails 
 we did not cover on our previous trip through the area heading east. We'll
  weave to the north side of the park\, and then make our way west to the G
 eorge Washington Memorial Park.\nWe'll do nearly a double loop in the big 
 cemetery\, and then make our way west to Harriett Wetherill Park. We'll do
  just about all of the trails there\, then make our way south onto a littl
 e piece of Cross County Trail\, followed by some back streets and communit
 y greenways in Plymouth Meeting.\nWe'll make our way from a neighborhood c
 onnection to Dixon Meadows Preserve and do their short trail. A final plea
 sant back road walk will take us to completed Wissahickon Green Ribbon Tra
 il\, which we will follow back to the start.\nDistance should be about 15 
 miles. If needed\, contact my cell at 908 343 8374
